e":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If you scale to a negative position at high speed, the selection on the left edge will be corrupted.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/feb9706f-5a64-404e-bd2b-f16a721cc529\r\n\r\n[scaledemo.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31338305/scaledemo.zip)\r\n\r\nI guess it's a timing issue with the checks.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5000831662","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5000831662"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488"}},"submitted_at":"2026-08-22T18:53:39Z","commit_id":"5d73829e813317d520d6f9e44d332c0ff71bfd7d"},{"id":5000950148,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKhRxhA","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Overall it's a desired feature and the code looks reasonable given how we use a similar design for moving a box selection. But I am running into issues trying to use the feature.\n\nI have the magnet icon \"Apply Snapping to selected keys\" button turned on (which is default).\nThis is the behavior I expect: When I use box scaling in other applications to scale keys, keys are aligned based on the FPS.\n\nBut with this PR, it seems like anything goes and keys are sped up or slowed down but not lined up with the framerate, even though I have snapping turned on.\n\nTo fix this, it will introduce lots of questions about how to deal with duplicate snapped keys which end up at the same timestamp. These issues also come up even without snapping, if you scale near 0 ratio, so it needs to be solved either way.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5000950148","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5000950148"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488"}},"submitted_at":"2026-08-22T20:09:07Z","commit_id":"5d73829e813317d520d6f9e44d332c0ff71bfd7d"},{"id":5329916548,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPbAShA","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It still seems to be unstable.\n\nCase left <= 0:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/463c6c07-2f0e-4129-8ac6-6db4ea5a529c\n\nCase right <= left\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d63bb72-613f-4436-911c-ba9bfec880b1\n\nI haven't thoroughly read the code yet, but I think the logic should probably be structured such that the scaling unit is determined first based on things like track display width and resolution, and then it calculates how many multiples of that unit to scale based on mouse movement, incorporating deterministic scaling and limitations.\n\n","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5329916548","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112488#pullrequestreview-5329916548"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112488"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-27T10:25:07Z","commit_id":"221293c5c79d805b5d3bc8a0c833c40bec1164da"},{"id":5585752526,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTO_Rzg","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?u=a4c48457845ad8e3e6c882efee5759a0a4da3033&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{